# Paths left OUT of the launch tarball (task1/ as the platform ships it to a VM).
#
# RULE (BUILD.md P9; DLI brief 1.5, Dana, Feb 26 2026): the override compose IS
# applied at launch. Every bind-mount source the override names must therefore
# either be in this tarball or be superseded by a named volume on the same
# container path in docker-compose.deployment.yml (the deployment file is
# merged last, so its named volume wins; `docker compose config` with all three
# files shows the result). As shipped:
#   /dli/task        lab, course-prep, assessment -> `task` volume (deployment wins);
#                    lab/task still ships, exactly as in Berlin, so a launch that
#                    merges the override last still finds the content.
#   /dli/assessment  assessment, override only    -> `assessment` volume (deployment
#                    wins), so assessment/ stays out and the answer keys never
#                    land on the VM's disk (the V1 house pattern).
#   /dli/prep        no mount at all: prepare_course.py is image content
#                    (lab/Dockerfile `COPY lab/prep /dli/prep`, BUILD.md 5a
#                    decision 6). lab/prep ships in the tarball only because P9
#                    forbids lab/** patterns here; nothing on the VM reads it.
# CI (.gitlab-ci.yml checks:platform) fails if the three-file merge leaves any
# bind mount under /dli. Never add lab/task or lab/** patterns to this file.
#
# Stays IN (do not list): docker-compose*.yml, .env, data_sources,
# load-course-data.py, nginx.conf (bind-mounted into nginx), deploy/ (its
# *-checkpoint.json files are bind-mounted into the loader; the directory ships
# whole), dind/ (ships whole), lab/task (and lab/prep, inert; see above).

# Used in build. Not required for deployment. (Dockerfile and entrypoint.sh are
# the template's inert lines: this course's live under lab/ and ship.)
Dockerfile
.launchignore
.dockerignore
.gitignore
entrypoint.sh

# Configures automatic deployment for builds. Not used by task.
vm_properties.json

# Included in container build. Not needed in launch tarball. assessment/ is
# superseded by the deployment file's named volume (rule above); task/* is the
# template's inert line (this course's content is lab/task, which ships).
assessment/*
task/*

# Host-side tooling, never on a learner VM (the additions BUILD.md P9 allows).
tests/*
**/__pycache__
**/.ipynb_checkpoints

# Contains secrets (dev only); production injects /dli/secrets/.env.
.env-dev
